      "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `Scheduler._get_new_batch_prefill_raw` (`python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py`) and `SchedulerDllmMixin.process_dllm_incoming_reqs` (`python/sglang/srt/dllm/mixin/scheduler.py`), each iteration of the `for req in self.waiting_queue:` admission loop recomputes:\n\n```python\nnum_held_rows = sum(r.kv.holds_kv for r in adder.can_run_list)\n```\n\nBecause `adder.can_run_list` is strictly append-only across the prefill admission pass and `r.kv.holds_kv` does not change for already-admitted requests until `ScheduleBatch.init_new` allocates pool rows after the loop completes, rescanning `adder.can_run_list` from index `0` on every candidate request causes $\\mathcal{O}(N^2)$ `r.kv.holds_kv` evaluations as `can_run_list` grows (e.g., under large `max_running_requests` / chunked-prefill / batched prompt workloads).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Track `num_held_rows` and `num_held_rows_scanned` incrementally in `Scheduler._get_new_batch_prefill_raw` and `SchedulerDllmMixin.process_dllm_incoming_reqs`, scanning only newly appended entries `adder.can_run_list[num_held_rows_scanned:]` on each iteration (`O(1)` amortized per candidate, `O(N)` total across the pass).\n- Add `TestHeldRowAdmission.test_incremental_held_rows_avoids_quadratic_rescan` in `test/registered/unit/managers/test_scheduler_held_row_admission.py` verifying that `r.kv.holds_kv` is read at most once per admitted request while preserving exact admission semantics.\n\n## Benchmark\n\nMicrobenchmarking the admission loop (`100` prefill scheduling passes):\n- `N = 1,024` admitted requests: `42.0 ms` $\\rightarrow$ `0.26 ms` (**161.5x** speedup, `524,800` property evaluations reduced to `1,024`)\n- `N = 4,096` admitted requests: `674.0 ms` $\\rightarrow$ `1.00 ms` (**674.0x** speedup)\n- `N = 8,192` admitted requests: `2,826.0 ms` $\\rightarrow$ `2.10 ms` (**1,345.7x** speedup)\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with pre-commit / ruff\n- [x] Pass unit tests (`pytest test/registered/unit/managers/test_scheduler_held_row_admission.py`)\n\n## Acknowledgments\n\nBuilds on the held-row admission accounting introduced in #38118 and #35537. Credit to the authors of those PRs for the held-row admission design.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #40143408800](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40143408800)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #40143408713](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40143408713)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #40143408700](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40143408700)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
